      "name": "Ordered Catalog Row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "ordered-catalog-row",
      "description": "Lists a real learning track with its index and local progress metadata.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-course-row\" href=\"#/track/react\"><span class=\"ds-course-index\">01</span><span class=\"ds-course-copy\"><strong>React</strong><small>Thành phần, state và luồng dữ liệu</small></span><span class=\"ds-course-state\">12 / 24 câu</span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-course-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 38px minmax(0,1fr) 112px; gap: 14px; align-items: center; padding: 14px 8px 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 72%, transparent); color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; } .ds-course-row:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-2) 74%, transparent); text-decoration: none; } .ds-course-row:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; } .ds-course-index { padding-left: 10px; border-left: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font: 12px/1.2 var(--mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; } .ds-course-copy { display: flex; min-width: 0; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; } .ds-course-copy strong { font: 650 1.05rem/1.35 var(--sans); } .ds-course-copy small { overflow: hidden; color: var(--muted); font: 400 13px/1.4 var(--sans); } .ds-course-state { color: var(--muted); font: 400 12px/1.4 var(--sans); text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; } @media (max-width: 760px) { .ds-course-row { grid-template-columns: 30px minmax(0,1fr); gap: 10px; padding: 13px 4px 13px 0; } .ds-course-state { grid-column: 2; text-align: left; } }"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Sổ thực hành",
    "overview": "Bovabon Edu is a Vietnamese learning space for developers reviewing programming and IT English. Its visual language borrows the useful parts of a study notebook: warm paper, clear section order, narrow margin marks, and tabular exercise numbers. Real course and local progress data remain the focus; paper is a color and organizational cue, not a texture or prop.\n\nThe catalog behaves like a printed contents page that opens into a digital lesson. The interface favors ruled rows, readable type, and a single clear next action. It avoids the dashboard of repeated metric tiles, uniform catalog cards, decorative gradients, and faux paper grain chosen against in the direction brief.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm ivory surfaces and charcoal text, with moss reserved for navigation and primary actions.",
      "Ordered course and exercise rows instead of a repeated card grid.",
      "Progress shown from the learner's local browser data and described as local.",
      "Flat surfaces; borders and spacing carry most of the hierarchy.",
      "Responsive navigation and content that remain usable at narrow widths."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink-on-Paper Rule",
        "body": "Keep body copy on a warm paper surface and use color to mark meaningful actions or learning states, never as a substitute for state text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Explicit Night Rule",
        "body": "Dark colors apply only after the learner chooses the dark theme; operating-system preference does not silently change the notebook default.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Lesson Rule",
        "body": "Keep lesson explanations at the stable 16px body size; reserve larger type for page and section hierarchy.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-By-Default Rule",
        "body": "Do not add shadows to catalog rows or ordinary lesson sections; reserve the existing shadow for overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the named palette and font stacks from the frontmatter.",
      "Do show real catalog counts and locally stored progress; explain where progress is saved.",
      "Do keep course and exercise discovery in readable, ordered rows.",
      "Do use sentence-case labels and numeric metadata that can be scanned quickly.",
      "Do preserve keyboard focus visibility, mobile drawer focus behavior, and local theme choice."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn the home catalog into a repeated dashboard card grid.",
      "Don't add fake paper grain, notebook props, hero gradients, or decorative metric tiles.",
      "Don't imply that learner progress is synced to an account or another device.",
      "Don't use color alone to convey pass, fail, warning, or selection states.",
      "Don't let tables or code samples make the page wider than its viewport."
    ]
  }
}
